Tutorials 2–4 followed [Workflow A](/en/usages/workflows/#workflow-a): a shared
site and event, with each cataloger recording the specimens they sorted. Most
small-mammal fieldwork also uses
[Workflow B](/en/usages/workflows/#workflow-b): each person runs their own trap
line, then prepares and catalogs its catch on their own device. Nobody else
needs that line's site or event until the catalogs are merged.

In this tutorial, **Bima** works independently on Line 2, creating its site and
event on his own device and cataloging one specimen from it. Nothing is shared
with Heru until [Teamwork tutorial 6](/en/tutorials/teamwork/merge-catalogs/).

| | Workflow A (Tutorials 2–4) | Workflow B (this tutorial) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Where specimens come from | Line 1, worked by both teammates | Line 2, worked by Bima |
| Who creates the site and event | Heru, then shares them | Bima, on his own device |
| What the merge does with them | Matches existing records | Adds them as new records |
| Field IDs | Each cataloger's own series | Each cataloger's own series |

## 1. Create Bima's site

On **Bima's device**, follow [Basic tutorial 3](/en/tutorials/basic/sites/) to
create the site.

{% steps %}

1. Open `Sites` and select `+`.
2. Enter `TJBS-L2` as `Site ID`, select `Bima Sampel` as `Site Leader`, and
   choose `Trapline` as `Site Type`.
3. Under `Geography`, select `Find existing locality` and choose the Pondok
   Merah locality that arrived with Heru's sites. Reusing it keeps one shared
   locality for all three lines.
4. Enter the same habitat description as `TJHH-L1`, and add
   `Most snap traps set 1–2 m above the ground.` to `Remarks`.
5. Add the `TJHH-PM` coordinate from
   [Basic tutorial 3](/en/tutorials/basic/sites/#3-add-the-coordinate).

{% /steps %}

{% devicepair
   phone="app-screenshots/tutorials/teamwork/iphone-site-tjbs-l2.webp"
   phoneAlt="NAHPU Sites page on an iPhone for TJBS-L2 with site leader Bima Sampel, site type Trapline, and the geography Indonesia, Jambi, Kerinci; the page counter reads page 3 of 3"
   phoneLabel="Bima · iPhone" /%}

The Site ID includes the line leader's initials (`BS`), following the
[Site ID convention](/en/usages/sites/). Because each line leader uses their
own initials, two teammates cannot accidentally create the same Site ID.

## 2. Create Bima's collecting event

{% steps %}

1. Open `Events` and select `+`.
2. Choose `TJBS-L2` as `Site ID`, and set `Start Date` to 12 September 2014 and
   `End Date` to 18 September 2014.
3. Set `Primary activity` to `Collecting`, and add the note explaining the
   `07:00` overnight capture-time convention from
   [Basic tutorial 4](/en/tutorials/basic/events/).
4. Add `Snap trap` with `Count` `25`.
5. Add the team: Bima Sampel (`Leader`), and Citra Contoh and Heru Handika
   (`Helper`).

{% /steps %}

{% devicepair
   phone="app-screenshots/tutorials/teamwork/iphone-event-tjbs-l2.webp"
   phoneAlt="NAHPU Events page on an iPhone for TJBS-L2-2014-09-12, site TJBS-L2, from 12 to 18 September 2014, with no start or end time"
   phoneLabel="Bima · iPhone" /%}

Pick Citra and Heru from the personnel list that arrived with the shared
events. While you can create new personnel on your own device when needed, we
recommend sharing existing teammates across devices so every device uses the
same UUID; recreating a teammate independently causes the merge to treat the
duplicate as a different person.

## 3. Catalog the catch from Line 2

On 13 September, Line 2 caught one *Maxomys hylomyoides*. On paper it is
HH 456, the specimen from
[Basic tutorial 5](/en/tutorials/basic/specimens/#hh-456-a-changed-identification)
whose identification was changed from *Mus crociduroides*. Here, Bima catalogs
it as `BS5`:

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Field ID | `BS5` (paper: HH 456) |
| `Taxon` | *Maxomys hylomyoides*, `ID Confidence` `Medium` |
| Site and event | `TJBS-L2`, `TJBS-L2-2014-09-12` |
| Capture date and time | 13 September 2014, `07:00` |
| `Method`, `Collector` | `Snap trap`, Bima Sampel |
| TTL–TL–HF–Ear, weight | 221–113–28–16, 48 g |
| `Sex`, `Life stage` | `Male`, testes abdominal; `Subadult` |
| Parts | `Whole body` in `Formalin`; `Liver` in `ETOH`, `Tissue ID` `Z26250` |
| `Remarks` | `First recorded in the field as Mus crociduroides.` |

If *Maxomys hylomyoides* is not yet in Bima's taxon registry, add it by
scanning Heru's taxon QR, as in
[Teamwork tutorial 3](/en/tutorials/teamwork/share-events-and-taxa/#2-copy-the-taxa-bima-needs).

## 4. Check the catalog before merging

Bima's device now holds two kinds of records:

- **Shared with Heru (Workflow A):** sites `TJHH-L1` and `TJHH-P1`, their
  events, and specimens `BS1` to `BS4`.
- **Created independently (Workflow B):** site `TJBS-L2`, its event, and
  specimen `BS5`.

Both go into the same project export. During the merge, NAHPU matches the
shared records to Heru's copies and adds Bima's own line as new, so mixing the
two workflows requires no extra steps.

{% aside type="tip" title="When a teammate needs your line before the merge" %}
If Heru needs `TJBS-L2` on his device (e.g., to help check its traps), Bima
can share its site and event using the same QR and JSON steps from Tutorials 2
and 3. The merge will then match them instead of adding them as new.
{% /aside %}

